# TTP-2026-0145 — AD CS ESC1 Certificate-Template Abuse — SAN-Mismatch Enrollment to PKINIT Privileged Auth (Cortex Identity ABIOC)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## BIOC — ITDR-017 AD CS Certificate-Template LDAP Reconnaissance
# severity: medium
# Certipy / Certify enumerate AD CS by issuing broad, repeated LDAP queries for pKICertificateTemplate objects, the PKI-Enrollment-Service container, and msDS-KeyCredentialLink. This BIOC keys on LDAP server search (event 1644) and LDAP client search (event 30) whose search filter references those AD CS / shadow-credential object classes from an account that does not normally perform certificate administration — the reconnaissance that precedes an ESC1 request.

dataset = ad_audit
| filter event_id in (1644, 30)
| filter search_filter contains "pKICertificateTemplate" or search_filter contains "pKIEnrollmentService" or search_filter contains "msDS-KeyCredentialLink"
| comp count_distinct(search_filter) as adcs_ldap_queries by host_name, subject_user_name, client_ip
| filter adcs_ldap_queries >= 2
| fields host_name, subject_user_name, client_ip, adcs_ldap_queries

## BIOC — ITDR-017 ESC1 Certificate Request With Enrollee-Supplied SAN
# severity: high
# A certificate request (Windows Security event 4886) against a template whose flags include CT_FLAG_ENROLLEE_SUPPLIES_SUBJECT where the requester supplies a Subject Alternative Name UPN that differs from their own account. This is the ESC1 enrollment step — the requester is choosing the identity the certificate will authenticate as. Evidence-grade catch keyed to the exact template-flag and the requested SAN.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id = 4886
| filter certificate_template_flags contains "CT_FLAG_ENROLLEE_SUPPLIES_SUBJECT"
| filter requested_san_upn != null and requested_san_upn != requester_domain_user
| comp count() as esc1_requests by ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, requested_san_upn, certificate_template
| filter esc1_requests >= 1
| fields ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, requested_san_upn, certificate_template, esc1_requests

## BIOC — ITDR-017 Certificate Issued With Requester-Subject SAN Mismatch
# severity: high
# The deterministic, evidence-grade signature of successful ESC1: Windows Security event 4887 records the CA issuing a certificate whose Requester does not equal the Subject / Subject Alternative Name. A low-privileged account has just been issued a certificate that authenticates as a different (privileged) principal. The certificate serial number and template are captured as citable forensic evidence for the POV report.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id = 4887
| filter requester_domain_user != subject_alt_name_upn
| comp count() as mismatched_issuances by ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, subject_alt_name_upn, certificate_template, certificate_serial_number
| filter mismatched_issuances >= 1
| fields ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, subject_alt_name_upn, certificate_template, certificate_serial_number, mismatched_issuances

## BIOC — ITDR-017 Shadow-Credential Write To msDS-KeyCredentialLink
# severity: high
# Optional persistence step — a Directory Service Changes event 5136 modifying the msDS-KeyCredentialLink attribute on a user or computer object by a non-administrative subject. Writing a key credential (shadow credential) grants durable, passwordless PKINIT re-entry as the target, extending the ESC1 compromise. Evidence-grade catch keyed to the attribute name and a non-admin subject.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id = 5136
| filter attribute_ldap_display_name = "msDS-KeyCredentialLink"
| filter subject_user_name not in ("Administrator", "SYSTEM")
| comp count() as shadow_cred_writes by host_name, subject_user_name, object_dn
| filter shadow_cred_writes >= 1
| fields host_name, subject_user_name, object_dn, shadow_cred_writes

## ABIOC — ITDR-017 ESC1 Issuance-To-PKINIT Privileged Impersonation Chain (behavioral-ML, causality-anchored)
# severity: high
# behavioral_profile: machine-learning
# causality_anchor: Learned identity baseline (the acting account never enrolls a certificate whose SAN is a different, privileged principal) -> a requester-to-subject SAN-mismatch certificate issuance (4887) -> a PKINIT TGT (4768, pre-auth type 16) authenticating as the SAN principal within seconds, the issuance-to-PKINIT lineage anchored on the impersonated identity.
# The auto-tuned terminal ABIOC anchors on a learned identity baseline in which the requesting account never enrolls certificates whose Subject Alternative Name is a different, privileged principal. It fires when a SAN-mismatch issuance (event 4887, requester != subject) is immediately followed within a short window by a PKINIT Kerberos TGT (event 4768, pre-authentication type 16) authenticating AS the very principal named in that SAN — the privilege-inheritance moment of ESC1. Every command is a legitimate certificate operation, so the catch comes from the LINEAGE (who requested a privileged-SAN cert, and that the cert was immediately used to authenticate as that privileged principal) rather than any known-bad signature. The issued certificate serial numbers and the impersonated UPN are surfaced as citable evidence.

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter event_id in (4887, 4768)
| alter impersonated_principal = coalesce(subject_alt_name_upn, target_user_name)
| filter (event_id = 4887 and requester_domain_user != subject_alt_name_upn) or (event_id = 4768 and pre_authentication_type = "16")
| comp count_distinct(event_id) as chain_stages, values(certificate_serial_number) as issued_serials, values(ca_host_name) as ca_hosts, min(_time) as first_seen, max(_time) as last_seen by impersonated_principal
| filter chain_stages >= 2
| fields impersonated_principal, ca_hosts, issued_serials, first_seen, last_seen, chain_stages

## VALIDATION — ITDR-017 Validate SAN-Mismatch Certificate Issuance
# purpose: validation
# dataset: msft_windows_security

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 900)
| filter event_id = 4887
| filter requester_domain_user != subject_alt_name_upn
| comp count() as mismatched_issuances by ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, subject_alt_name_upn, certificate_serial_number
| filter mismatched_issuances >= 1
| fields ca_host_name, requester_domain_user, subject_alt_name_upn, certificate_serial_number, mismatched_issuances

## VALIDATION — ITDR-017 Hunt PKINIT Authentication Following Anomalous Certificate Issuance
# purpose: hunt
# dataset: msft_windows_security

dataset = msft_windows_security
| filter _time > to_timestamp(current_time() - 3600)
| filter event_id in (4768, 4769)
| filter pre_authentication_type = "16"
| comp count() as pkinit_events by host_name, target_user_name, event_id
| filter pkinit_events >= 1
| fields host_name, target_user_name, event_id, pkinit_events

